-- A BECAUSE that starts a line of its own belongs to the `#ASSERT REFUSED`
-- above it only when it is indented further than the `#ASSERT`. Here it is at
-- the left margin, so it is a parse error, at the BECAUSE.
--
-- The service evaluates a module with its directives taken out, line by line,
-- and a directive's lines end at the first line that is neither blank nor
-- indented further than the directive. A BECAUSE at the margin would be left
-- behind there, so the parser and the service would read it differently.

GIVETH A NUMBER
`nope` MEANS REFUSE "the real reason"

#ASSERT REFUSED `nope`
BECAUSE "the real reason"
